  "verdict": "AT AROMATIC_LO=1.30 THE HEAD IS HIGH-PRECISION/LOW-RECALL (P=0.887, R=0.287, F1=0.434). TIGHTENING THE BAND TO 1.45 TRADES PRECISION FOR RECALL (P=0.258 -0.629, R=0.447 +0.160, F1=0.327 -0.107) AND TO 1.50 SHARPENS THE TRADE (P=0.123 -0.764, R=0.731 +0.444, F1=0.211 -0.223). F1 IS MAXIMISED AT 1.30, the current threshold. THE HEAD'S 5539 AROMATIC PREDICTIONS ARE CONCENTRATED IN BO 1.30-1.50 (4912 of 5539 = 88.7% fall inside [1.30, 1.70)); tightening the band relabels those 'correct' predictions as 'false positive' rather than 'correct' and F1 falls. THE COLLAPSE IS RELOCATED, NOT FIXED: the constant edit would lower F1, not raise it. The binding axis is the head's intrinsic over-prediction of aromatic on lower-BO bonds, not the band boundary."
